## Key Coverpoints (ExceptionsH-SN)

- `cp_hedeleg` — medeleg × hedeleg × 8 faults × 5 priv modes; GVA bit
- `cp_ecall_to_vs/hs/m` — status bits on trap (SPP, SPV, SPVP, MPV, MPP, GVA)
- `cp_virtual_instruction_vs/vu` — all virtual-instruction trigger paths
- `cp_loadstore_priv` — HLV/HSV legal in M/HS; virtual-instr in VS/VU; illegal in U if HU=0
- `cp_hfence_priv` — SFENCE/HFENCE.VVMA/HFENCE.GVMA by priv + TVM/VTVM
- `cp_xtinst_*` — mtinst/htinst behavior per exception type

## Key Coverpoints (InterruptsH-NC)

- mideleg bits 10,6,2 (and 12 if GEILEN>0) read-only 1
- hideleg writable bits 10,6,2 only
- Interrupt cause translation: VS ext(10)→guest SEI(9), VS timer(6)→STI(5), VS soft(2)→SSI(1)
- Priority: SEI > SSI > STI > SGEI > VSEI > VSSI > VSTI > LCOFI
- hip.VSEIP = OR(hvip.VSEIP, hgeip[VGEIN], platform)
- hip.VSTIP = OR(hvip.VSTIP, vstimecmp vs time+htimedelta)

## Key Coverpoints (SvH-US)

- vsatp/hgatp MODE/PPN/ASID/VMID WARL
- Two-stage read/write/ifetch across page sizes
- G-stage: all accesses as U-mode; guest-page fault not page fault
- VS MXR overrides VS-stage only; HS MXR overrides both stages
- World switch: zero vsatp → swap hgatp → write new vsatp

## SvH-US Test Environment Defaults

- H extension enabled; two-stage when applicable
- vsatp tests: hgatp.MODE=Bare; hgatp tests: vsatp.MODE=Bare
- Run in VS-mode unless stated; SFENCE.VMA / HFENCE after PT changes
- Valid PTE perms: XWRV=1111, A/D=11 unless otherwise specified

